# This private key is PUBLIC ON PURPOSE. It is not a secret and it never was.
# The filename does not say so, this header does: this key is committed to the
# repository and everyone has it.
#
# It exists so that anyone who clones this repository can build and flash AkidaTag
# firmware immediately, with no setup step. It is for development only. Because it
# is published here, a signature made with it proves nothing about who produced the
# firmware; treat any image signed with it as untrusted.
#
# BrainChip's released firmware is NOT signed with this key. Official releases are
# signed with .env/production_key.pem, a different key that is genuinely private
# and is not in this repository in any form.
#
# Leave this file as it is. If you want your own boards to trust only your own
# firmware, generate a key of your own into this directory under a name of your
# own and point SB_CONFIG_BOOT_SIGNATURE_KEY_FILE in src/sysbuild.conf at it. See
# src/README.md, "Application Security", for the full recipe and for how a board
# moves between keys.
